The sum is even exactly when both rolls are even or both are odd. There are $3 \cdot 3 = 9$ ordered even-even pairs and $3 \cdot 3 = 9$ ordered odd-odd pairs, so $18$ of the $36$ ordered pairs give an even sum.

Among those $18$ pairs the two rolls agree on the six values $1$ through $6$, giving $6$ pairs.

P(\text{same} \mid \text{even sum}) = \frac{6}{18} = \frac{1}{3}
